`renvor new`'s help. The reserved flags are `hide = true`, so they must NOT appear here — a user
should not be offered a flag that is guaranteed to fail. They are still accepted and refused with a
message naming the phase; see `exit-codes.trycmd`.

```
$ renvor new --help
Create a project, from prompts or from flags.

With a terminal, `renvor new` asks only the questions this phase can honour and shows a review
screen before writing anything. Without one, it takes the same answers as flags. Generation is
transactional: a failure before placement leaves the destination untouched.

Usage: renvor[EXE] new [OPTIONS] [NAME]

Arguments:
  [NAME]
          Project name. Defaults to the destination's final component

Options:
      --output <human|json>
          Result format for stdout
          
          [default: human]

      --path <PATH>
          Where to create the project. Defaults to `./<name>`

      --target <TARGET>
          What to generate. `api` is the only supported value in this phase
          
          [default: api]

      --yes
          Accept confirmations. Never waives validation

      --dry-run
          Compute and report without writing anything

      --local-domain <LOCAL_DOMAIN>
          Local development domain. Defaults to `<name>.test`

      --container
          Generate container development controls

      --no-color
          Disable styling. Styling is also off automatically when the stream is not a terminal

      --local-https
          Record that local HTTPS is wanted. **Issues nothing and modifies no trust store.**

      --example-domain
          Generate the example domain module

      --seed-data
          Generate seed data. Requires `--example-domain`

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

```
